{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"private-gentled-morpho","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`output_mode` (src/rebar/llm/structured.py:43) blanket-forces PromptedOutput whenever\n`thinking=True`, and its docstring (:50-56) states the rationale: \"pairing extended thinking\nwith a native/forced output constraint is the documented Anthropic 400\". E1 (recorded on the\nselection bug ticket) measured that rationale stale: the historic 400 was tool_choice x\nthinking; `outputConfig` json_schema + thinking succeeds on the wire today (sonnet adaptive,\nhaiku budget 2048). The blanket guard therefore forces the prompted path — the very path this\nepic exists to harden — even on cells where native output is measured-safe under thinking.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a capability field `native_output_with_thinking: bool = False` to the capabilities model\nin src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py (fail-closed default). Change the guard in `output_mode` to:\nNativeOutput iff `caps.native_structured_output` AND (`not thinking` OR\n`caps.native_output_with_thinking`). Rewrite the docstring to the measured facts, including\nthat tools x thinking x native suppresses tool calling (E1: 2/2 skipped) — which is why this\nfunction's single call site, src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:181, is the no-tools single-shot\npath and the agentic runner never consults it; the no-tools scoping is structural, not a\nparameter. No behavior changes in THIS ticket: every existing capability record keeps the\ndefault False, so thinking still forces prompted everywhere until the rows story adds measured\ncells. That keeps this slice independently landable with pure contrast tests.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/structured.py — the guard + docstring in `output_mode`\n- src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py — the new field (default False)\n- tests/unit/test_structured.py (or the capabilities test file) — contrast tests\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier, config-effect contrast through the real read path (shared test-design standard §6):\n\n- caps(native=True, with_thinking=True) + thinking=True -> NativeOutput (new behavior gate).\n- caps(native=True, with_thinking=False) + thinking=True -> PromptedOutput (default preserved;\n  negative control proving no cell flips in this ticket).\n- caps(native=True) + thinking=False -> NativeOutput; caps(native=False) -> PromptedOutput\n  (both existing branches pinned unchanged).\n- Mutation check: reverting the guard to the blanket `not thinking` form turns the first test\n  RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The four contrast cases above pass — checked by the new unit tests.\n- [ ] No existing test changes: the current suite passes unmodified, proving zero behavior\n      change at defaults — checked by `make test`.\n- [ ] The docstring states the measured facts (tool_choice x thinking as the historic 400;\n      tool-suppression as the no-tools scoping reason) and cites the E1 evidence location —\n      checked in code review.","id":"0fa4-a836-5f13-4a44","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Gate output_mode on measured thinking-compatibility per model"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785891881658224001,"uuid":"3439a237-aa3f-4236-bb76-3a323f9c0053"}